{"type": "root", "attrs": {"index": "no"}, "body": [{"level": 0, "type": "title", "indent": 0, "text": ["Work with mattes"], "extent": [12, 33]}, {"type": "warning_group", "body": [{"ext": null, "type": "warning", "indent": 0, "text": ["Old network"], "role": "item", "extent": [16, 38], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 4, "text": ["As of Houdini 20.5, use ", {"scheme": null, "value": "/nodes/cop/index", "type": "link", "text": ["Copernicus nodes"], "fullpath": "/nodes/cop/index.html"}, " instead of Compositing nodes. Though both networks still exist, the Compositing network is now designated as ", {"type": "code", "text": ["COP Network - Old"]}, ". The Compositing network and its nodes will be deprecated and then removed in a future Houdini release."], "extent": [38, 335]}], "container": true}], "container": true, "role": "item_group"}, {"type": "para", "indent": 0, "text": ["A ", {"type": "em", "text": ["matte"]}, " is a grayscale image you use as either an alpha channel or a\n", {"scheme": null, "value": "/composite/masks", "type": "link", "text": ["mask"], "fullpath": "/composite/masks.html"}, "  to isolate certain parts of the image."], "extent": [77, 213]}, {"type": "para", "indent": 0, "text": ["For example, if you wanted to crop an image inside a hexagon shape, you\nwould create a hexagonal matte and connect it to the node\u2019s ", {"scheme": null, "value": "/composite/masks", "type": "link", "text": ["mask\ninput"], "fullpath": "/composite/masks.html"}, " ."], "extent": [213, 378]}, {"type": "para", "indent": 0, "text": [{"scheme": "Image", "value": "/images/matte_1.png", "type": "img", "text": ""}], "extent": [378, 407]}, {"type": "para", "indent": 0, "text": ["Mattes can be simple (a shape or a gradient) or complex, based on the\ncolors in the image you want to use the matte on."], "extent": [407, 528]}, {"type": "task_group", "body": [{"ext": null, "type": "task", "indent": 0, "text": ["Generate mattes"], "role": "item", "extent": [528, 551], "body": [{"type": "bullet_group", "body": [{"blevel": 6, "type": "bullet", "indent": 4, "text": ["See  ", {"scheme": null, "value": "shapes", "type": "link", "text": ["how to create shapes"], "fullpath": "/composite/shapes.html"}, " ,\n      ", {"scheme": null, "value": "fills", "type": "link", "text": ["gradients"], "fullpath": "/composite/fills.html"}, " , and  ", {"scheme": null, "value": "keying", "type": "link", "text": ["generate mattes based on image\n      colors (keying)"], "fullpath": "/composite/keying.html"}, " ."], "extent": [551, 690], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 6, "text": ["You can also  ", {"scheme": null, "value": "noise", "type": "link", "text": ["add noise"], "fullpath": "/composite/noise.html"}, "  to a matte to give it\n      some variation."], "extent": [690, 774]}], "container": true}], "container": true}], "container": true}, {"ext": null, "type": "task", "indent": 0, "text": ["Use a matte to isolate part of an image"], "role": "item", "extent": [774, 821], "body": [{"type": "bullet_group", "body": [{"blevel": 6, "type": "bullet", "indent": 4, "text": ["Connect the matte to a node\u2019s  ", {"scheme": null, "value": "/composite/masks", "type": "link", "text": ["mask input"], "fullpath": "/composite/masks.html"}, " ."], "extent": [821, 891]}, {"blevel": 6, "type": "bullet", "indent": 4, "text": ["Connect the image to the first input of a ", {"scheme": "Node", "value": "/nodes/cop2/switchalpha", "type": "link", "text": ["Switch Alpha\n      node"], "fullpath": "/nodes/cop2/switchalpha.html"}, ", and connect the matte to the\n      second input. The Switch Alpha operator copies the second\n      input to the alpha channel of the first input. Turn on the\n      ", {"type": "ui", "text": ["Redo premultiply"]}, " parameter to override any previous\n      premultiplication."], "extent": [891, 1234]}, {"blevel": 6, "type": "bullet", "indent": 4, "text": ["Use the ", {"scheme": "Node", "value": "/nodes/cop2/premultiply", "type": "link", "text": ["Premultiply operator"], "fullpath": "/nodes/cop2/premultiply.html"}, " to use a\n      matte stored in a plane of the image you want to isolate. Use\n      the name of the matte plane in the ", {"type": "ui", "text": ["Alpha"]}, " parameter."], "extent": [1234, 1433]}, {"blevel": 6, "type": "bullet", "indent": 4, "text": ["Connect the image to the input of the node generating the\n      matte. In the ", {"type": "ui", "text": ["Image"]}, " tab of the matte node\u2019s parameter\n      editor, change the ", {"type": "ui", "text": ["Add image"]}, " parameter to ", {"type": "q", "text": ["C (RGB)"]}, " and\n      ", {"type": "q", "text": ["Multiply"]}, "."], "extent": [1433, 1646]}], "container": true}], "container": true}, {"ext": null, "type": "task", "indent": 0, "text": ["Shrink or enlarge mattes"], "role": "item", "extent": [1646, 1678], "body": [{"type": "bullet_group", "body": [{"blevel": 6, "type": "bullet", "indent": 4, "text": ["Use the ", {"scheme": "Node", "value": "/nodes/cop2/expand", "type": "link", "text": ["Expand"], "fullpath": "/nodes/cop2/expand.html"}, " or ", {"scheme": "Node", "value": "/nodes/cop2/dilateerode", "type": "link", "text": ["Dilate\n      Erode"], "fullpath": "/nodes/cop2/dilateerode.html"}, " operator to shrink or enlarge mattes."], "extent": [1678, 1803], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 6, "text": ["The Dilate Erode operator is faster, but does not provide good\n      quality for large changes. The Expand operator is slower, but\n      produces higher quality."], "extent": [1803, 1972]}], "container": true}], "container": true}], "container": true}, {"ext": null, "type": "task", "indent": 0, "text": ["Adjust edges and falloff of a matte"], "role": "item", "extent": [1972, 2015], "body": [{"type": "bullet_group", "body": [{"blevel": 6, "type": "bullet", "indent": 4, "text": ["Because mattes are just grayscale images, you can use the full\n      complement of image-manipulation tools in the compositor to\n      adjust mattes."], "extent": [2015, 2172], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 6, "text": ["Use the ", {"scheme": "Node", "value": "/nodes/cop2/gamma", "type": "link", "text": ["Gamma operator"], "fullpath": "/nodes/cop2/gamma.html"}, " to reduce falloff at\n      the low end (gamma < 1) or high end (gamma > 1)."], "extent": [2172, 2296]}], "container": true}, {"blevel": 6, "type": "bullet", "indent": 4, "text": ["Use an ", {"scheme": "Node", "value": "/nodes/cop2/expand", "type": "link", "text": ["Expand operator"], "fullpath": "/nodes/cop2/expand.html"}, " with zero size and a\n      small ", {"type": "ui", "text": ["Dropoff"]}, " to add a bit of falloff to a map."], "extent": [2296, 2424]}, {"blevel": 6, "type": "bullet", "indent": 4, "text": ["Use the ", {"scheme": "Node", "value": "/nodes/cop2/blur", "type": "link", "text": ["Blur operator"], "fullpath": "/nodes/cop2/blur.html"}, " with a Gaussian blur to\n      soften a matte. You can also use the ", {"scheme": "Node", "value": "/nodes/cop2/edgeblur", "type": "link", "text": ["Edge Blur\n      operator"], "fullpath": "/nodes/cop2/edgeblur.html"}, ", which blurs based on edge\n      detection and so may preserve fine details of the map better."], "extent": [2424, 2678]}], "container": true}], "container": true}, {"ext": null, "type": "task", "indent": 0, "text": ["Combine mattes"], "role": "item", "extent": [2678, 2700], "body": [{"type": "bullet_group", "body": [{"blevel": 6, "type": "bullet", "indent": 4, "text": ["Use the  ", {"scheme": null, "value": "/composite/layers", "type": "link", "text": ["compositing operators"], "fullpath": "/composite/layers.html"}, "  to combine\n      mattes."], "extent": [2700, 2784], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 6, "text": [{"scheme": "Image", "value": "/images/matte_combine.png", "type": "img", "text": ""}], "extent": [2784, 2825]}, {"type": "para", "indent": 6, "text": ["To get the union of two mattes, use the\n      ", {"scheme": "Node", "value": "/nodes/cop2/screen", "type": "link", "text": ["Screen"], "fullpath": "/nodes/cop2/screen.html"}, ", ", {"scheme": "Node", "value": "/nodes/cop2/max", "type": "link", "text": ["Maximum"], "fullpath": "/nodes/cop2/max.html"}, ", or\n      ", {"scheme": "Node", "value": "/nodes/cop2/add", "type": "link", "text": ["Add"], "fullpath": "/nodes/cop2/add.html"}, " operator. To take the union but cut out\n      overlapping areas, use the ", {"scheme": "Node", "value": "/nodes/cop2/xor", "type": "link", "text": ["XOR operator"], "fullpath": "/nodes/cop2/xor.html"}, "."], "extent": [2825, 3062]}, {"type": "para", "indent": 6, "text": ["To get the intersection of two mattes, use the ", {"scheme": "Node", "value": "/nodes/cop2/min", "type": "link", "text": ["Minimum\n      operator"], "fullpath": "/nodes/cop2/min.html"}, ". To cut one matte out of another, use\n      the ", {"scheme": "Node", "value": "/nodes/cop2/subtract", "type": "link", "text": ["Subtract operator"], "fullpath": "/nodes/cop2/subtract.html"}, "."], "extent": [3062, 3243]}, {"type": "para", "indent": 6, "text": ["To use one operator to modulate another, use the ", {"scheme": "Node", "value": "/nodes/cop2/multiply", "type": "link", "text": ["Multiply\n      operator"], "fullpath": "/nodes/cop2/multiply.html"}, "."], "extent": [3243, 3347]}], "container": true}], "container": true}], "container": true}], "container": true, "role": "item_group"}], "title": ["Work with mattes"], "included": ["/composite/_old_cops_deprecated"]}